current_state:
  - MiniModel.org is the Rust-first P2P tiny model package exchange roadmap site.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face discovery, local Hugging Face conversion-request/script handoff, local share metadata and `.minimodel-share-kit.ps1` export after verified `.slm` import, Rust `inspect-share-metadata` validation for metadata-only and share-kit-ready TinyRustLM bundles, protected TinyRustLM NuGet SDK local share-kit verification that assembles manifest-declared pieces into a verified `.slm` plus `<output.slm>.p2p-import-receipt.json` and can inspect that receipt sidecar without network fetch or private routing, one-command `prepare-peer-share` sender packaging, companion-readable `write-peer-companion-state` share metadata plus Rust `inspect-peer-companion-state` revalidation, metadata-only `write-peer-contact-card` known-peer URL cards, Rust `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed` validation for metadata-only peer-source availability feeds with exact byte/SHA evidence and a 4 MiB pre-parse JSON budget, user-run `serve-peer-companion` state+piece/status serving including path-prefixed peer base URLs such as `/peer-pieces/`, manifest+peer-offer catalog-entry writing, late `add-peer-source` consenting peer metadata publication, portable `write-peer-source-announcement` metadata, `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` metadata publication, same-origin checksum-bound peer-source announcement feed routes via `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed`, maintainer-side `apply-peer-source-announcements` drift checks, batch `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` publication, metadata-only `write-catalog-snapshot` reuse, Rust `inspect-catalog-snapshot` preflight for existing `models.v0.json` snapshots with exact byte/SHA evidence and a 4 MiB pre-parse JSON budget, optional catalog-listed consenting peer sources, direct known-peer HTTP status/piece serve/fetch, one-command TinyRustLM peer-import request execution, local metadata-only `write-import-receipt-ledger` / `inspect-import-receipt-ledger` receipt indexes, later optional user-run MiniModel Peer Companion for advanced local peer duties, and future broader P2P discovery/relay; all converge on local `.slm` verification.
  - NuGet public publication status on 2026-07-06: local package-folder feed-current and feed-hash verification pass for `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, and `TinyRustLM.P2P` version `0.1.1`, but NuGet.org reports zero listed versions for all three package IDs; do not claim public NuGet.org availability until authenticated publish and NuGet.org feed-current/feed-hash verification pass.
  - Browser NuGet public-doc status on 2026-07-07: the branded `UAIX.Browser.Core.Abstractions`, `UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Runtime`, `UAIX.Browser.p2pRuntime.P2P`, `UAIX.Browser.Memory`, and `UAIX.Browser.p2pLLM.Conversion` lane is post-publish verified at `0.1.8`; MiniModel catalog-boundary docs mention `uaix-browser-nuget-release-readiness-publish-plan-dry-run.json` as the release-readiness dry-run path so routine audits preserve retained pushed-package evidence in `uaix-browser-nuget-publish-plan.json`. Local folder-feed audit, NuGet.org feed-current, SHA256SUMS-bound feed-hash verification, release-readiness `published_current`, and clean NuGet.org consumer smoke passed with `memory files 62`, `FileDeck.IncludesManifestJson`, and `conversion validated`.
  - MiniModel.org now carries one narrow TinyRustLM.com first-run public demo exception: `catalog/default-demo.v0.json` declares `minimodel.public_demo_model.v0` and points to `artifacts/demo/tiny-test-model-q8.slm`. The artifact is 8832 bytes with SHA-256 `6af985853325eaa6d3eaaa8aadd3511da9596eb542fb2d03a9bc9dc1f4377adf`, browser byte checksum `0xa338bbb579e3e971`, and `.slm` runtime/manifest checksum `0x481f1037d57ebcd3`. TinyRustLM.com may fetch only this tiny runtime-smoke `.slm` with credentials omitted, validate byte count/SHA-256 before Rust/WASM load, reach `Ready`, and generate. This does not make MiniModel.org a general hosted model-byte server; user/private models, peer pieces, premium weights, and converted artifacts remain local or P2P-reverified.
  - Live deploy status on 2026-07-07: `https://MiniModel.org/catalog/default-demo.v0.json` and `https://MiniModel.org/artifacts/demo/tiny-test-model-q8.slm` are post-deploy verified over HTTPS. The live catalog is 2026 bytes with SHA-256 `588f7e2ebfc28d34df0f083e6aa07dcf4220dabf3ef75673986c3666c9e3a41c`; the live artifact is 8832 bytes with SHA-256 `6af985853325eaa6d3eaaa8aadd3511da9596eb542fb2d03a9bc9dc1f4377adf`. Live TinyRustLM browser smoke with the local default-demo interceptor disabled fetched both real MiniModel.org routes and generated successfully.
  - MiniModel local peer serving now supports TinyRustLM live browser peer checks by returning browser CORS/PNA headers for metadata routes only: `minimodel.peer_status.v0.json`, the peer piece-set metadata route, and optional companion-state metadata. Piece chunk routes deliberately remain non-CORS so browser readiness checks cannot turn into model-byte fetches; receiver import still requires Rust reverify. The focused minimodel-core test `serves_browser_cors_only_for_peer_metadata_routes_when_fixture_present` passed.
  - `write-peer-companion-inventory` / `inspect-peer-companion-inventory` now provide a metadata-only companion inventory that binds a prepared share's companion state, manifest, peer-piece directory, sender-side receipt ledger, piece-store byte/quota/SHA-256 evidence, optional peer contact-card metadata, duplicate contact-card peer URL rejection, and a Rust-verified `ready-after-rust-reverify` serve plan without embedding model bytes or peer-piece payloads.
  - `write-peer-contact-book` / `inspect-peer-contact-book` now bundle 1-64 already reviewed `minimodel.peer_contact_card` files into metadata-only `minimodel.peer_contact_book.v0` JSON with embedded card SHA-256s, duplicate peer URL rejection, no model bytes, no peer-piece bytes, no catalog availability claims, and Rust reverify required before browser import.
  - TinyRustLM can load a local `minimodel.peer_companion_inventory.v0` in its P2P panels as metadata preview, reject no-byte-boundary and serve-plan drift, and show a Rust-reverify-required summary with the peer status route without making it a catalog availability claim.
  - Known peer URLs are strict direct `http://` URLs with plain DNS/IPv4 host text and safe absolute paths. MiniModel rejects project and Hugging Face canonical/www/subdomain/root-dot hosts, malformed dot hosts, query/fragment URLs, path traversal, whitespace, and control characters before manifest reads, output writes, or peer fetches; TinyRustLM's `peer-url-unsafe-ui` browser smoke now proves the browser fails closed on the same unsafe URL forms before accepting a normal path-prefixed loopback peer URL.
  - MiniModel manifest validation now supports `external-signature-v0` as the only signed envelope kind in addition to `unsigned-draft`; the verifier rejects unknown signature kinds, rejects comments in signed manifests, computes the canonical sorted non-signature manifest body, requires `signature.payload_sha256` to match that body, and prints the computed payload digest from `minimodel verify-manifest` for publisher/reviewer handoff. `minimodel verify-signed-manifest <manifest> <public-key-json>` now performs local Ed25519 verification against metadata-only `minimodel.public_key.v0` JSON, requiring matching publisher id, key id, public-key route, public-key SHA-256, manifest-signing usage, `revoked=false`, and an `ed25519-base64:` signature over the canonical payload; transparency-log and remote key-discovery policy remain later gates.
  - First implementation code now includes a Rust verifier workspace: `crates/minimodel-core` plus `crates/minimodel`, line-oriented manifest parsing, `serde_json` parsing for TinyRustLM peer-import request JSON, local share metadata bundles, and catalog snapshot validation, real q8 fixture manifest, local `.slm` artifact verification, chunk/Merkle checks, `inspect-share-metadata` validation for TinyRustLM metadata-only and `generated-local-minimodel-share-kit-v0` bundles with project-server-byte and chunk-list drift rejection, TinyRustLM `share-metadata-ui` smoke coverage that runs that Rust validator against actual browser-downloaded bundles, plus source and mapped public-root `share-metadata-import-ui` coverage proving local share metadata reimports as checksum-bound `Use Metadata` rows until generated catalog/manifest metadata exists with chunk-list drift rejection, wrong local `.slm` rejection, matching local `.slm` generation, and no remote model/catalog requests, one-command `prepare-peer-share` output from a local `.slm` into MiniModel manifest plus `.minimodel-peer-offer` plus local peer pieces plus catalog entry, companion-readable `write-peer-companion-state` output that validates a prepared share and consenting peer URL before writing metadata-only local state, standalone `inspect-peer-companion-state` output that revalidates state/manifest/piece-directory agreement and rejects piece-count or project-server-flag drift, `write-peer-contact-card` and `inspect-peer-contact-card` output that validate metadata-only direct known-peer URL cards with no model bytes and Rust-reverify-required flags, public `minimodel` CLI integration tests for share metadata inspection, prepare-peer-share sender packaging from the q8 fixture, offline `inspect-peer-import-request` validation of TinyRustLM receiver handoff JSON before network access, `inspect-import-receipt` validation of completed receipts against the manifest and assembled `.slm`, `write-import-receipt-ledger` and `inspect-import-receipt-ledger` local metadata-only receipt index validation with stale receipt-SHA drift rejection, live serve/check/preflight/import/receipt-inspect receiver execution through `serve-peer-companion`, strict UTC receipt/preflight timestamp parsing plus future-preflight chain rejection, companion-state writing from a prepared q8 share, metadata-only state/preflight/ledger boundaries, contact-card/book write/inspect output, peer companion inventory write/inspect output, peer-source announcement feed write/inspect output for prepared-share feeds, empty feeds, and project-server-flag rejection, catalog snapshot write/inspect output for normal and feed-bound snapshots plus project-server-flag rejection, path-prefixed/root-dot URL normalization, malformed host rejection, and project/Hugging Face host rejection before artifact/manifest reads or output writes, `serve-peer-pieces`/`serve-peer-companion` output that validates local share state before serving `minimodel.peer_status.v0.json` plus allow-listed piece routes and optional `minimodel.peer_companion_state.v0.json`, path-prefix serving for validated companion peer base URLs, `check-peer-status` output that fetches only peer-status metadata and writes a no-piece-byte readiness report, `inspect-peer-status-check` output that revalidates the saved report against the manifest, drift-checked `write-catalog-entry` output from manifest plus `.minimodel-peer-offer`, catalog snapshot rejection for incomplete import-ready peer-offer proof envelopes, `add-peer-source` output that validates a proof-ready entry and attaches one consenting direct peer URL, `write-peer-source-announcement` output that binds model id/artifact checksum/peer-offer route/chunk count/Merkle/proof checksum/catalog-entry checksum to one consenting peer URL, `apply-peer-source-announcements` output that rejects route/checksum/chunk-count/Merkle drift and deduplicates peer URLs before catalog publication, `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` output that validates zero or more portable announcements into a metadata-only feed, `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed` output that revalidates existing feed envelopes and hashes exact feed bytes, `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed` output that binds a same-origin feed route into `models.v0.json` by SHA-256, batch `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` output that validates entries plus announcements and rejects unmatched announcement model ids, metadata-only `write-catalog-snapshot` output after duplicate/model-byte/peer-source rejection, `inspect-catalog-snapshot` output that revalidates existing snapshots and hashes exact catalog bytes, optional `peer_source_count`/`peer_sources` metadata after known-peer URL validation, local peer-piece export, direct HTTP peer-piece serving/fetch with project/Hugging Face host rejection and optional companion-state validation when advertised, peer-piece reassembly, `import-peer-request` receiver execution, basename-only import receipts with peer-import transfer evidence plus receipt reinspection, and metadata-only import receipt ledgers for local companion/audit use.
  - TinyRustLM `share-metadata-kit-exec` coverage executes the exact browser-downloaded `.minimodel-share-kit.ps1` with `MINIMODEL_KNOWN_PEER_BASE_URL`, verifies generated MiniModel metadata plus local receipt-ledger output plus peer-companion inspection PASS output plus contact-card/book outputs, starts local `serve-peer-companion`, and runs `check-peer-status` with no peer-piece or artifact bytes fetched; the same smoke is now green against the packaged TinyRustLM.com root through mapped `http://tinyrustlm.com:<port>/`.
  - TinyRustLM `share-metadata-kit-exec` coverage also verifies peer companion inventory output and `inspect-peer-companion-inventory` PASS output for the generated share kit before local companion serving starts.
  - TinyRustLM local peer-source intake now labels `Peer-source announcement/feed JSON` and `hf-peer-announcement-ui` uses a real `peer-source-announcements.v0.json` feed envelope, proving maintainer-style announcement feeds can be applied to local proof-ready metadata before `P2P Import`.
  - `catalog/models.v0.json` now binds the metadata-only `catalog/peer-source-announcements.v0.json` feed by SHA-256 and can be revalidated with `minimodel inspect-catalog-snapshot`. `inspect-catalog-snapshot`, `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed`, and `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed` reject catalog/feed JSON above 4 MiB before parsing and report exact byte counts plus SHA-256 evidence. The current public feed is intentionally empty, so it proves availability checking without making any model P2P-ready before a real consenting peer source is published.
  - The July 2 TinyRustLM/MiniModel intake synthesis is routed as a durable constraint: Hugging Face rows are metadata only until local Rust conversion or P2P import, proof-ready rows are not called runnable, and converted-once availability is published through peer-source metadata without project servers hosting bytes.
  - GGUF source files can now pass through TinyRustLM's local `tinyrustlm-slm-pack inspect-gguf`, `plan-gguf-source`, `extract-gguf-source`, and `convert-gguf-trained` gates when tensors are supported F32/F16/BF16/Q2_K/Q3_K/Q4_0/Q4_1/Q4_K/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0/Q8_1/Q8_K payloads; GGUF conversion still requires supported tensor names/shapes, tokenizer token-count compatibility, and Rust validation before `.slm` import.
  - The July 3 desktop/P2P intake synthesis is routed as a durable constraint: an optional MiniModel Peer Companion may later manage local peer identity, piece stores, cache quotas, consent prompts, direct serve/fetch controls, receipts, and receipt ledgers, but it remains user-run software and does not make project servers host, proxy, cache, run, or serve user model bytes.
  - `docs/peer-companion.md` is the detailed future companion design and completion gate; it preserves local-only source lanes, shared Rust verifier contracts, consent gates, piece-store rules, test expectations, and the no-server-byte boundary.
  - `docs/peer-companion.md` now includes July 3 report triage: accepted engineering guidance includes multi-crate Rust boundaries, strict Tauri IPC/capabilities, actor/message-passing network workers, OS secure storage, local metadata stores, signed/checksummed releases, and domain-first tests; deferred lanes include WebTransport, WebRTC, mDNS, DHT/bootstrap, UPnP/NAT-PMP, Iroh/QUIC, Rust-libp2p, BitTorrent-style chunking, Pear, Bare, and Hypercore; rejected current-product lanes include project-operated STUN/TURN, relay, rendezvous, signaling, bootstrap, or DHT infrastructure as a default dependency and any project-server model-byte proxy/cache/serve/run path.
  - The live public-safe export is verified.
  - Direct public .uai and agent-file-handoff access is denied.
